#!bovnar 1.1
# A datetime carrying sub-second digits: the whole-second epoch count is the
# carrier and the ".123" is preserved verbatim in bovnar, but JSON has only the
# integer carrier, so converting this to JSON must be a hard error rather than a
# silent truncation of the fraction (regression fixture for cmd_convert).
.t = <datetime:64> 2026-06-15T12:00:00.123Z;
